      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Today, Google and Voltus announced an expanded agreement to build a 1-gigawatt (GW) virtual power plant across the PJM grid region, which serves 67 million people across 13 states and Washington, D.C.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/infrastructure-and-cloud/global-network/virtual-power-plant-1-gigawatt/",
        "source": "Google (The Keyword · AI)",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-22T15:11:08.441Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Voltus aggregates flexible capacity from local businesses and homes — like smart thermostats, batteries, and industrial assets — into a Google-funded virtual power plant.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/infrastructure-and-cloud/global-network/virtual-power-plant-1-gigawatt/",
        "source": "Google (The Keyword · AI)",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-22T15:11:08.441Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Building on a 100-megawatt agreement from earlier this year, this 10-fold expansion represents one of the largest known distributed capacity portfolios deployed by a hyperscaler to date.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/infrastructure-and-cloud/global-network/virtual-power-plant-1-gigawatt/",
        "source": "Google (The Keyword · AI)",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z",
